        <h2>The Strength Scale: How Snus &amp; Pouches Are Measured</h2>
        <p>Nicotine strength in oral products uses two measurements:</p>
        <p>
          <strong>mg/pouch (or mg/portion):</strong> The total nicotine contained in one pouch. This is the number
          that matters for your experience — it's what your body absorbs.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>mg/g (milligrams per gram):</strong> The nicotine concentration of the pouch material. This can
          be misleading — a small pouch with high mg/g delivers less total nicotine than a large pouch with lower mg/g.
        </p>
        <p>Always compare mg/pouch when evaluating strength across brands.</p>

        <h2>Complete Brand Strength Comparison</h2>

